2c23684c9cc5ef5899073b59844fa47cc3c1d894f2316e21f25d5d85be5a10e2

Current EvoCC refuses those independent cases with E2702/E2001/E2001,
respectively. The checked-in CLI regression requires refusal and empty output
for C-HIR execution, EvoIR emission and assembly emission: nine boundaries.
The four existing scalar/legacy atomic tests still pass. This is a capability
inventory with positive oracle controls, not three fixed compiler failures or
a concurrency proof. Scalar __atomic_load_n/store_n and legacy __sync RMW/CAS
are implemented; general atomic-C and the other __atomic interfaces are not.

Source/command inventory of the currently pinned application populations:

* SQLite 3.53.4 src/sqliteInt.h:238-239 uses only __atomic_load_n/store_n
  (relaxed) for AtomicLoad/AtomicStore. sqlite3.c and tsrc repeats are generated
  copies, not additional interfaces. Its current lane uses the supported path.
* TinyCC's captured 11 EvoCC objects exclude lib/bcheck.c and lib/stdatomic.c.
  Those files and tests/tests2/{125_atomic_misc,136_atomic_gcc_style}.c exercise
  the broader interfaces above; they belong to runtime/test configurations, not
  the 11-object compiler-build numerator. tccgen.c descriptions and tcctok.h's
  _Atomic keyword are compiler input data, not host atomic execution.
* zlib 1.3.2 zutil.h's Z_ONCE uses stdatomic.h/atomic_flag. crc32.c enables it
  with DYNAMIC_CRC_TABLE (also selected by MAKECRCH). The captured default
  crc32.o command in .build/ladder/zlib/build.log has neither option; it uses
  the static CRC table. An alternate dynamic-table build needs separate scope.
* musl's actual atomics use src/internal/atomic.h and arch/aarch64/atomic_arch.h;
  its current first refusal is the retained strict-fenv option, not a missing
  __atomic RMW declaration.
* Bounded lexical census of C/header sources in the pinned torture execute,
  c-testsuite, LLVM SingleSource, Csmith base/bitfields, jq, Lua, zstd, cJSON,
  Mbed TLS, PolyBench and toybox trees finds no further occurrences of
  __atomic_*, _Atomic or stdatomic.h. The census uses rg --no-ignore so ignored
  build trees are included. This is not a claim about uncaptured configurations,
  vendor headers, future versions or all code produced by a tested C compiler.

